Fixed the email list, the providers control panel, a user's account panel, the sign-in methods page and the provider icon upload in projects whose install gives `@plone/components` a different copy of `react-aria-components` from the add-on's. The pages failed with "Cannot destructure property 'selectionBehavior'", and the icon's "Choose a file" button did nothing. The add-on's `razzle.extend.js` now resolves `react-aria-components` the way `@plone/components` resolves it, so both always use one copy, whatever the project's lockfile holds. `react-aria-components` is now an optional peer dependency, and `@plone/components` is accepted from 4.2.1 onwards instead of only at that exact version. @ericof
